# React Three Fiber & 3D

When editing R3F/Three.js files:

- Apply engineering foundations first (always-applied rule).
- Load `skills/code/web/libs/threejs/SKILL.md` for render-loop, typing, shader, and disposal rules.
- Load its `references/` and `assets/r3f-component-template.tsx` only when the skill directs.
- Follow the nearest `AGENT.md` chain for the project's 3D folder layout and orchestration wiring.

Key rules: never allocate inside `useFrame`, mutate uniforms/refs per frame (no `setState`), type materials/refs concretely, dispose geometries/materials/textures, prefer drei + `InstancedMesh`.
